WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.750
Part 1 of Masters of the Universe: Revelation
ends on a huge cliffhanger with the fate of

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.810
He-Man and Skeletor revealed, and hidden in
the first five episodes are a stack of clues

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.019
you might have missed which also predict what
could happen next.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:18.930
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing all the crucial details

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.750
from the new Netflix He-Man series plus theories
for Part 2!

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.619
Many thanks to World of Tanks for sponsoring
this video.

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:28.410
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.980
The ending of Part 1 sees Adam, Teela and
her band of heroes return to Eternia with

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.120
the Sword of Power reforged thanks to Roboto's
heroic sacrifice.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.160
The sword had been split in two when He-Man
used it to absorb the exploding Orb of Power

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.140
that Skeletor cracked open at the beginning
of the series.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.460
The energy from the orb not only killed Adam,
but also nearly all the magic that held Eternia

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.690
together vanished when each half of the Sword
of Power disappeared to Preternia and Subternia,

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.690
aka Heaven and Hell.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:02.190
So when Adam holds the restored sword aloft
and says "By the power of Grayskull", he's

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.190
able to call back the Power and reinstate
magic in Eternia.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:11.360
The Hall of Wisdom becomes Castle Grayskull
again and the Orb of Power is restored and

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.360
locked away.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.971
However, just as Adam is about to complete
the phrase and transform into He-Man, Skeletor

00:01:16.971 --> 00:01:21.820
makes a surprise return and stabs Adam through
his midriff with his Havoc Staff.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.200
Skeletor, like He-Man, vanished when the Orb
of Power exploded in the first episode, and

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.420
he reveals that to avoid being completely
destroyed by the blast, he hid his essence

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.549
in Evil-Lyn's wand staff.

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:38.580
Skeletor's trick was hinted at a number of
times in earlier episodes such as when Evil-Lyn's

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.120
orb lit up mysteriously and when it began
whispering at one point.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.900
[otherworldly whispers]
And Teela funnily enough was unwittingly closer

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.930
to the truth than she realised when she made
a jibe at Evil-Lyn in the third episode:

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.260
Take no life advice from the likes of Evil-Lyn,
Andra.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.000
Remember, she's the only one here carrying
around a Skeletor in her closet.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.720
So, after Skeletor's shocking defeat of He-Man
– which must be the first time in the animated

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.439
franchise's history – the villain takes
the Sword of Power for himself, and says the

00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:14.700
magic words which transform him into a god
version of himself, Skelegod.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.700
Now I...

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:21.239
Skeletor...
am Master of the Universe!

00:02:21.239 --> 00:02:27.610
Now, let's talk about that possibly lethal
stabbing that Skeletor landed on Adam.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.219
Notice the location of the wound which is
roughly around the same place

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:35.450
- in the middle of the body –
where Adam stabbed Skeletor in the first episode

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.939
and we know that he managed to survive that.

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:42.549
You finally used that sword the way it was
meant to be used.

00:02:42.549 --> 00:02:48.139
By the way, Skeletor's line there is a nod
to how in the Filmation animated series, He-Man

00:02:48.139 --> 00:02:53.290
never used his sword in a violent way against
his opponents and, as a kids' show, the series

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:57.069
as a whole also shied away from serious violence.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:01.650
Masters of the Universe: Revelation is a continuation
of the 80s series, however, it's clearly a

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:06.260
lot darker with real fights taking place between
the characters with some of them even trying

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.829
to kill each other.

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:12.739
And given this darker path for the new series,
I think that initially in Part 2 Adam could

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:14.709
well be confirmed dead.

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:19.439
This would hit particularly hard as he was
told before he left Preternia that his next

00:03:19.439 --> 00:03:22.269
death would probably not allow him back into
Heaven.

00:03:22.269 --> 00:03:24.319
If you were to return to Eternia...

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:27.099
You might never be able to come back here.

00:03:27.099 --> 00:03:30.249
You would end as mortals do:
in dirt.

00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:36.349
However, there is precedence for He-Man dying
in the franchise, specifically the He-Man/Thundercats

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:41.059
comic book crossover where Adam also died
and came back to life.

00:03:41.059 --> 00:03:45.219
After being brutally stabbed with the Sword
of Power in the books, Adam was initially

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:50.839
able to heal his mortal wounds by holding
onto the sword while saying his classic catchphrase.

00:03:50.839 --> 00:03:56.659
Later, however, Adam died but was resurrected
after being entombed with the Sword of Power.

00:03:56.659 --> 00:04:01.229
In the Netflix show, we might see something
similar in Part 2, with Teela and the other

00:04:01.229 --> 00:04:06.019
heroes banding together again, this time to
find a way to take the Sword of Power from

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:07.549
Skeletor and revive Adam.

00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:12.279
Evil-Lyn might also be a key part of that,
which I'll talk more about shortly.

00:04:12.279 --> 00:04:17.750
Orko is another major character who appeared
to die, but I suspect he might not have.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.200
In the Land of the Dead episode, Orko confronted
his fears that he'd never be able to control

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.780
his magical abilities.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:29.490
As he and the team tried to leave Subternia,
Scare Glow arrived to attack them one final

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.490
time.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.600
In a display of magical mastery, Orko froze
the falling rocks that were about to land

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.820
on Teela and the others, then bravely fended
off Scare Glow, giving them an opportunity

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.820
to escape.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:40.820
Look!

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:41.820
I'm doing it!

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.820
I'm not afraid.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.590
He can't scare me.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.040
Orko then trapped Scare Glow with his magic
rings and tried to blast him away.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.660
Demon be gone...

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.470
Go back to your shadow!!

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:58.460
The resulting explosion saw Orko and Scare
Glow vanish, while throwing Teela and co through

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:03.450
the portal to Preternia, with just a fragment
of Orko's cloak floating through the door

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.620
as it closed.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.340
When Adam discovered what happened, he built
a memorial stone to honour his fallen friend,

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:13.180
assuming that he'd died;
however, I don't think that's the case.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.121
In fact, Orko's battle with Scare Glow in
the underworld may have actually turned the

00:05:17.121 --> 00:05:20.610
his character into a much darker version for
Part 2.

