00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.550
To understand why we may be getting Dark Orko
in Part 2, we need to look at what happened

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:39.200
to Orko in the DC Universe vs The Masters
of the Universe comics.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.190
In that comic book storyline, Orko ended up
absorbing an evil force when he tried to destroy

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:48.940
the Skull of Power, and that unlocked the
mental barriers that had been holding him

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.640
back, transforming him into Dark Orko.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.460
That's an interesting parallel with what happens
to Orko in the Land of the Dead where he explained

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:01.680
how he struggled with magic when he was young,
but then we see him master it in his showdown

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.090
with Scare Glow.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:07.530
During that crucial battle, Orko summoned
an immense amount of magic and tried to banish

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.150
the villain, similar to how he tried to destroy
the Skull of Power in the comics.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:16.810
That attempt to defeat Scare Glow, who was
holding onto Orko during the explosion which

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:21.870
followed, may have transformed the Trollan
into something else, for example if he absorbed

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.770
some of the evil being's megalomaniac traits
and wicked powers.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:30.270
The gold rings that Orko conjured during his
encounter with Scare Glow are similar to the

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:34.230
fiery rings of magic that Dark Orko uses in
the comic.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:39.020
And the shadow beasts that attack Orko and
Evil-Lyn in Subternia are a little reminiscent

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.330
of the horde that Dark Orko unleashes in the
books.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:47.580
We might find that, in Part 2 of Revelation,
Dark Orko has replaced Scare Glow as the ruler

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.760
of the underworld, commanding an army of shadow
monsters himself now.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:56.540
I think introducing Dark Orko could add another
intriguing element to the show as it would

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:01.460
be quite unexpected and in keeping with the
darker themes and tone of the new series.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.510
My other big prediction for Part 2 and beyond
is that although Evil-Lyn switched back to

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:11.180
Skeletor's side, she may end up betraying
him and even helping the good guys again in

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.180
the future.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.360
I really was starting to like you kids.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:18.700
Perhaps Evil-Lyn thought it was best to feign
she was still loyal to her villainous boss

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.610
in that moment, with a view to potentially
usurping him at a later point.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:26.300
After all, she regretted some of the time
she'd spent working for him.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:31.550
Instead of fulfilling my destiny, I spent
a lifetime helping him fulfill his.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:37.829
In the 80s animated series, Evil-Lyn sometimes
carried out her own schemes independent of

00:08:37.829 --> 00:08:38.829
Skeletor.

00:08:38.829 --> 00:08:42.360
In fact, in the episode "The Witch and the
Warrior", when Lyn found herself having to

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:45.713
work with Teela, she revealed that what she
was really after was her own power.

00:08:45.713 --> 00:08:47.449
I have no loyalty to Skeletor, it is power
I want.

00:08:47.449 --> 00:08:52.220
Someday, I'll seize it from him.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:57.720
I very much expect that at some point in Revelation,
Evil-Lyn will end up being full-on resentful

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.889
of being Skeletor's sidekick.

00:08:59.889 --> 00:09:04.200
On top of that, I think she may have grown
genuinely fond of Teela and the gang, and

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.749
we saw a glimpse of that when she opened up
to Orko during their time together in the

00:09:08.749 --> 00:09:09.749
underworld.

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:13.290
No, they didn't call me "Evil,"
I added that part later.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:16.410
[chuckles]
Lyn also used the last of her magic to conjure

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:21.480
the doorway that would take them all from
Subternia to Preternia, which Orko said proved

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.720
that she might not be so bad deep down.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.199
Turns out nobody's born evil.

00:09:26.199 --> 00:09:31.519
If Skeletor doesn't give Lyn any real opportunities
for power in Part 2, which I don't expect

00:09:31.519 --> 00:09:37.259
he will now he's Skelegod, I think she may
well end up turning against him and even helping

00:09:37.259 --> 00:09:39.329
Teela out as well.

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:43.290
We also need to talk about Teela, as there
are many hints to a secret side of her that

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.560
hasn't yet been fully revealed.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.630
In fact, there were several moments in Part
1 where somebody was about to reveal a big

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:53.630
secret about her but they got cut off:
There's something I have to tell you...

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.630
Oh, no.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.630
We don't have time.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.290
Because you have a special--
Don't you understand?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.290
Teela.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.290
There's... there's something--
[Teela] Don't.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.290
I don't want to hear it.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:04.290
The secret that everyone seems to want to
tell Teela is that

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.630
- spoiler alert -
her mother is the Sorceress of Castle Grayskull.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:12.640
This was something revealed to Teela in the
second episode of the Filmation series.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:20.779
You are my own daughter and someday you will
take my place as the mystic guardian of Grayskull.

00:10:20.779 --> 00:10:24.139
At the time, however, the Sorceress decided
to wipe Teela's memory of this knowledge.

00:10:24.139 --> 00:10:26.059
For now you have other deeds to do.

00:10:26.059 --> 00:10:28.470
You must forget what you have learned today.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:32.420
And this secret is why the Sorceress calls
Teela to Castle Grayskull when she fears she

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.319
may die during Skeletor's attack.

00:10:34.319 --> 00:10:37.769
I wanted to see you, Teela, one last time.

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:38.769
Me?

00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:42.329
We see how Teela has been avoiding dealing
with a sense that's she's different when the

00:10:42.329 --> 00:10:45.439
evil version of herself confronts her in Subternia.

00:10:45.439 --> 00:10:51.600
Pretending to be ordinary when you know, deep
down, you are so much more.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.740
And how that must terrify you...

00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:00.189
Teela admits to Scare Glow that she's never
understood her power, but then proves her

00:11:00.189 --> 00:11:04.420
connection to her magical heritage as she
manifests the missing piece of the Sword of

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.800
Power by herself.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.560
What...
are you?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:12.450
Notice these three marks that appear on Teela's
forehead momentarily as she creates the sword

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.079
as I think we'll see those again in the future.

00:11:15.079 --> 00:11:19.949
As the original Filmation series suggests,
Teela may take over from her mother the Sorceress

00:11:19.949 --> 00:11:24.410
as the Guardian of Grayskull, should she ever
die or need to step down.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.879
And although Teela was able to call on her
power that one time in the underworld, she

00:11:28.879 --> 00:11:33.370
will need to fully embrace her magical side
if she wants to take over that role.

